    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0364" n="232" xml:id="pg232"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/7–745: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 199 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on the Allied Commission on
                        Reparations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pauley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d199-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]<anchor n="2" xml:id="d199-f2"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-07T20:00:00+03:00">July 7, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2466. Top secret to the Secretary from Pauley.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I consider it most important that the agenda of the coming conference provide for
                    consideration of these reparation matters<anchor n="3" xml:id="d199-f3"/> as
                    well as the question of the inclusion of France.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d199-f4"/>
                    You would favor me greatly if you would see that these matters are given a high
                    place on the agenda as they are questions of high policy which must be
                    determined.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d199-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d199-f1-content">
                <p>Sent over the signature of Harriman. Sent to Washington; relayed to Byrnes, then
                    at sea, in telegram No. 9 of July 9 (file No. 740.00119 (Potsdam)/8–645).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d199-f2" n="2" xml:id="d199-f2-content">
                <p>For the full text of this message, see <ref target="#d370">document No.
                    370</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d199-f3" n="3" xml:id="d199-f3-content">
                <p>For the details of the matters referred to, see <ref target="#d370">document No.
                        370</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d199-f4" n="4" xml:id="d199-f4-content">
                <p>i. e., in the Allied Commission on Reparations.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
